===============================================================
Installing ONIE on EC2 x86_64 Virtual Machine (copied from KVM)
===============================================================

Cross-Compiling ONIE
====================

Change directories to ``build-config`` to compile ONIE.

To compile ONIE first change directories to ``build-config`` and then
type ``"make MACHINE=ec2 all"``.  For example::

  $ cd build-config
  $ make -j4 MACHINE=ec2 all recovery-iso

When complete, the ONIE binaries are located in
``build/images``::

-rw-r--r-- 1 dn dn 11925880 Dec 18 18:45 ec2-r0.initrd
-rw-r--r-- 1 dn dn  4969120 Dec 18 18:30 ec2-r0.vmlinuz
-rw-r--r-- 1 dn dn 37486592 Dec 18 18:50 onie-recovery-x86_64-ec2-r0.iso
-rw-r--r-- 1 dn dn 16836602 Dec 18 18:45 onie-updater-x86_64-ec2-r0

ec2-r0.vmlinuz -- This is the ONIE kernel image

ec2-r0.initrd  -- This is the ONIE initramfs (filesystem)

onie-updater-x86_64-ec2-r0 -- This is the ONIE self-update
image.  This image is a self-extracting archive used for installing
ONIE.

onie-recovery-x86_64-ec2-r0.iso -- This is a recovery ISO image
that can be installed as a CDROM image.

